==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hʌŋˈɡɛɹiənʔnoʊteːʃən/}}

===Etymology===
The notation was invented by {{w|Charles Simonyi}} (born 1948), Hungarian-American computer programmer.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|head=[[Hungarian]] [[notation]]}}

# {{context|computing|programming}} A naming convention in which the [[name]] of a [[variable]] indicates its [[data type]] and intended use by including [[abbreviation]]s as [[prefix]]es.
#: ''<code>lpsz</code> is '''Hungarian notation''' for a 32-bit pointer to a null-terminated string.''

